text:
The sun was hot, and he sat down under the tree ;

And on his head it fell from the sky with a thud;

And so she shut her eyes for a moment to see what came;

When a strange little creature jumped out of its shade ;

"Twas the night before Christmas, and all through

the house,

Not a creature was stirring — not even a mouse;

The leaves are brown and bare, but now is winter’s time ;

And little winds with glee will shake their rustle through them;
As when some wildwood bird has broken into rhyme ,

Or when the autumn winds have blown among the pines.
